{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"5e12f1fbadddd304ce9715599dd489e8b328c8f66381f9faeee20259e4ef3cac","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_803622eab5e4535d1f4c47bc20e56347d8ef21792ceb9593a3414714fc8a7891","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a strong technical contribution to semi-supervised learning but has significant policy and compliance issues. The most critical issue is the violation of double-blind review policies due to the inclusion of author names, affiliations, and emails. Additionally, the lack of a broader impact statement and ethical considerations is a notable weakness. The use of standard public datasets is appropriate, but explicit licensing information would strengthen the paper's compliance with data usage policies.","paper_id":"BJ6oOfqge","paper_identity_sha256":"76c65c4dfb9c69e4419c25f058568d611ce5734994cc2f6e68168ab65271bc2e","prompt_identity_sha256":"6d773fa4f4c4158b22981f24be7718e9155f48b694398aa74cd80e5931e25bfb","raw_response_sha256":"c7d7841ad2814db836a6f6cf0b3865f1ab913af8d0f8136bacfeb6ffe6bdb72d","request_identity_sha256":"20b75956463aa2eaa73dea78fbcd20accd62ebffeb269adae411092605d82be1","reviewer_identity_sha256":"6832030d37bc6b05f4de12f913ecdea182594ad5d7ac3dcd33edcb54d7bd3a1a","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v2","structural_context_sha256":"ec8cc86da9d81ce8a38b5be410cca5062f602d489d08646f9fd3ed8657b0909d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-002","SRC-022"],"review_text":"The paper does not include a dedicated section on ethics, fairness, or potential harms. While the method is applied to standard image classification benchmarks (CIFAR-10 and SVHN), which are generally low-risk datasets, the lack of discussion on broader ethical implications, such as the potential for bias in classification tasks or the societal impact of deploying such models, is a notable omission. The authors do discuss tolerance to incorrect labels, which is a positive aspect for robustness, but this does not substitute for a broader ethical impact statement.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-015","SRC-018","SRC-019"],"review_text":"The paper uses two standard public datasets: CIFAR-10 and SVHN. Both datasets are widely used in machine learning research and are typically available under permissive licenses that allow for research use. The paper does not explicitly state the license terms or provide links to the datasets, but given their standard nature in the field, it is reasonable to assume compliance with data usage policies. There is no indication of personally identifiable information (PII) or privacy concerns, as the datasets consist of synthetic or non-sensitive images (house numbers and generic objects).","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The paper clearly identifies the authors (Samuli Laine and Timo Aila) and their affiliation (NVIDIA) on the first page. This is a violation of double-blind review policies, which require the removal of author names, affiliations, and any other identifying information to ensure an unbiased review process. The presence of author emails (slaine@nvidia.com, taila@nvidia.com) further compromises anonymity.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-004","SRC-022","SRC-023"],"review_text":"There is no evidence of plagiarism or dual submission in the provided text. The paper cites relevant prior work, including the ladder network (Rasmus et al., 2015) and bootstrapping methods (Reed et al., 2014), and clearly distinguishes its contributions from these existing methods. The related work section is thorough and appropriately credits previous research.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-002","SRC-027"],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement or a checklist addressing the societal implications of the work. While the method is primarily technical and applied to standard benchmarks, the absence of a discussion on the potential broader impact, such as the environmental cost of training large models or the societal implications of improved classification accuracy, is a weakness. Additionally, there is no mention of software or data licensing details, which could be important for reproducibility and compliance.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"6f4e3741889c19f83d8097ce7c9e873c87bc03e3ed57dee53daaa062876f6ace","paper_id":"BJ6oOfqge","paper_ordinal":21,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"c7d7841ad2814db836a6f6cf0b3865f1ab913af8d0f8136bacfeb6ffe6bdb72d","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"BJ6oOfqge","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"77c8f4f2b845bfa96f29bc0b4ce883eea66327078fa38db9cd215892125d75f2","request_identity_sha256":"20b75956463aa2eaa73dea78fbcd20accd62ebffeb269adae411092605d82be1","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v2","usage":{"completion_tokens":878,"prompt_tokens":14830,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":15708},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"20b75956463aa2eaa73dea78fbcd20accd62ebffeb269adae411092605d82be1","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v1"}